          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Calorons are topologically non-trivial
            = succeed "-configurations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} positive temperature
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \gt 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T =  0
            are called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPST+instantons"} BPST instantons
            (but there is no continuous limit relating the two).
          %p
            While the physical reality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            is at best subtle (they are interpreted as witnessing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+tunneling"} quantum tunneling
            between actual
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} positive temperature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotation
            has good physical meaning at positive temperature.
          %p More in detail:
          %p
            Upon
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotation
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{3,1}
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KMS+state"} KMS state
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is expressed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+field+theory"} Euclidean field theory
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi β
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \times S^1_{\beta}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            and the second factor is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"} length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ≔
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \coloneqq 1/T
            (proportional to) the inverse
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/temperature"} temperature
          %p
            A
            %em caloron
            is a
            = succeed "-configuration" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi β
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \times S^1_\beta
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
            the topological class of these bundles (their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^2 \times S^1 \longrightarrow G
          %p hence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^3 \times S^1 \longrightarrow B G
          %p
            For the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU(2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq S^3
            and via the usual math/physics translation of terminology (
            %a{:href => "BPST-instanton#FromTheMathsToThePhysicsStory"}> here
            ) this was first considered in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HarringtonShepard77"} Harrington-Shepard 77, p. 3
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HarringtonShepard78"} Harrington-Shepard 78, p. 1
          %p
            A further refinement of the construction included the nonzero
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+expectation+value"} vacuum expectation value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 4
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle (A_4)^3\rangle
            of the “time” component of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+potential"} vector potential
            %em KvBLL caloron
            (
            %a{:href => "#KraanVanBaal98a"}> Kraan-van Baal 98a
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KraanVanBaal98b"} Kraan-van Baal 98b
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LeeLu98"} Lee-Lu 98
          %p
            This solution revealed the substructure: it gets split into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c
            (number of colors) separate (anti)self- dual 3d solitons with nonzero (Euclidean) electric and magnetic charges (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LarsenShuryak14"} Larsen-Shuryak 14
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToConfinement Relation to confinement
          %p
            As part of a possible solution to the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            = succeed "-problem:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap"} mass gap
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Greensite11"}> Greensite 11, section 8.5
            \:
          %blockquote
            %p
              it is natural to wonder if
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              could be derived from some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiclassical+approximation"} semiclassical
              treatment of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang%E2%80%93Mills+theory"} Yang–Mills theory
              based on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
              solutions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"} non-abelian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPST+instanton"} standard
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "BPST-instanton#BelavinPolyakovSchwartzTyupkin75"} 40
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strengths"} field strengths
              fall off too rapidly to produce the desired magnetic disorder in the vacuum.
            %p
              In recent years, however, it has been realized that instanton solutions at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} finite temperature
              = succeed "," do
                %em calorons
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#KraanVanBaal98"} 41
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#KraanVanBaal98b"} 42
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#LeeLu98"} 43
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
              constituents which may, depending on the type of caloron, be widely separated.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              The caloron idea is probably the most promising current version of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              in pure non-abelian gauge theories, but it is basically (in certain
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauges
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
              with spherically symmetric abelian fields, and this leads to the same questions raised in connection with monopole Coulomb gases.
          %h3#relation_to_heterotic_string_theory Relation to heterotic string theory
          %p
            The
            %em gauge solution
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            contains a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            on the transverse space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPST-instanton"} BPST-instanton
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3\times S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/caloron"} caloron
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sasaki-Yata16"} SasYat16, pag.12
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\rightarrow 0
            we obtain a smeared
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The paper
            %a{:href => "#Harrington-Shepard_78"} Harrington-Shepard 1978
            considers the contribution from periodic solutions at
            %em positive, finite
            temperature to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+equations"} Yang-Mills equations
            to the action of a ‘Yang-Mills gas’: an equilibrium ensemble of YM fields. They give explicit solutions to the classical equations of motion ‘of charge 1’ i.e. representing a generator in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            classifying topologically inequivalent solutions.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Werner+Nahm"} Nahm
            (
            %a{:href => "#Nahm_84"}> Nahm 1984
            ) continued the study of calorons, linking them with self-dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADHM+construction"} ADHM construction
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"}> instanton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soliton"} soliton
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortex"} vortex
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} thermal field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/caloron+correspondence"} caloron correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nahm+transform"} Nahm transform
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The concept was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#HarringtonShepard77
              %p
                Barry J. Harrington, Harvey K. Shepard,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Euclidean solutions and finite temperature gauge theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(77)90413-8"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(77)90413-8
            %li#HarringtonShepard78
              %p
                Barry J. Harrington, Harvey K. Shepard,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Periodic Euclidean solutions and the finite-temperature Yang-Mills gas
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.17.2122"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.17.2122
          %p Further development includes
          %ul
            %li#Nahm_84
              %p
                W. Nahm,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Self-dual monopoles and calorons
                %strong 201
                (1984) pp 189-200. doi:
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0016145"} 10.1007/BFb0016145
            %li#KraanVanBaal98a
              %p
                Thomas C. Kraan, Pierre van Baal,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Periodic Instantons with non-trivial Holonomy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805168"} arXiv:hep-th/9805168
            %li#KraanVanBaal98b
              %p
                Thomas C. Kraan, Pierre van Baal,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Exact T-duality between Calorons and Taub-NUT spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802049"} arXiv:hep-th/9802049
            %li#LeeLu98
              %p
                Kimyeong Lee, Changhai Lu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                    Calorons and Magnetic Monopoles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802108"} arXiv:hep-th/9802108
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caloron"} Caloron
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
          %ul
            %li
              P. Gerhold, E.‐M. Ilgenfritz, M. Müller‐Preussker, B. V. Martemyanov, A. I. Veselov,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Topology and confinement at
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo ≠
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \neq 0
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.2714375"} doi:10.1063/1.2714375
          %h3#relation_to_skyrmions_instantons_monopoles Relation to skyrmions, instantons, monopoles
          %p
            The construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahManton89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              , N S Manton,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Skyrmions from instantons
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(89)90340-7
          %p
            The relation between
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmions"} skyrmions
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calorons"} calorons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            is usefully reviewed and further developed in
          %ul
            %li#Cork18a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Josh+Cork"}> Josh Cork
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calorons, symmetry, and the soliton trinity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://etheses.whiterose.ac.uk/22097/"} web
            %li#Cork18b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Josh+Cork"}> Josh Cork
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Skyrmions from calorons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04143"} arXiv:1810.04143
          %h3#in_confinementmass_gap In confinement/mass gap
          %p
            Discussion as part of a solution to the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            = succeed "-problem:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap"} mass gap
          %ul
            %li#Greensite11
              %p
                Jeff Greensite,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Introduction to the Confinement Problem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-3-642-14382-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-14382-3
            %li
              %p
                P. Gerhold, E.-M. Ilgenfritz, M. Müller-Preussker,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    An
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                    KvBLL caloron gas model and confinement
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0607315"} arXiv:hep-ph/0607315
            %li#LarsenShuryak14
              %p
                Rasmus Larsen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"} Edward Shuryak
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classical interactions of the instanton-dyons with antidyons
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 950
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.6563"} arXiv:1408.6563
            %li#LarsenShuryak15
              %p
                Rasmus Larsen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Shuryak"} Edward Shuryak
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interacting Ensemble of the Instanton-dyons and Deconfinement Phase Transition in the SU(2) Gauge Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.03341"} arXiv:1504.03341
          %h3#relation_to_ns5brane_in_heterotic_string_theory Relation to NS5-brane in heterotic string theory
          %ul
            %li#SasakiYata16
              Shin Sasaki and Masaya Yata,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Non-geometric five-branes in heterotic supergravity
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1611
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.01436"} arXiv:1608.01436
        .revisedby
